      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The interaction was studied of homeostatic lipids of the membrane components in the blood plasma as was the correction thereof and condition of the bodily immune processes in patients with unstable angina pectoris (UAP). A total of fifty UAP patients were treated with lipid. Utilization of the lipid modulus was found out to have a striking immunoregulation effect. Activation of the phagocytic link of the immune response was noted to be on the decrease, the disbalance of the regulatory lymphocyte subpopulations getting less, which facts result in lowering of the autoantibodies production, normalization of blood free radical processes and pronounced clinical effect in the above patient population."},
